# server.py is the RENDER entrypoint (render.yaml runs `uvicorn server:app`),
# where it serves both the static site and the API from one process. On VERCEL
# the model is different — static files in public/ + each api/*.py as its own
# serverless function — and server.py must NOT be uploaded: Vercel would build
# its FastAPI `app` as a catch-all function that intercepts /api/* and crashes
# on import (StaticFiles(directory="public") can't resolve from /var/task).
server.py
render.yaml

# Dev-only — not needed by the serverless functions, keeps the bundle lean.
tests/
evals/
.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
